<DocsLayout title="LlamaIndex guide | dotfetch" description="Integrate dotfetch with LlamaIndex: per-step tool selection for FunctionAgent, failures as error ToolOutputs, human-in-the-loop approval and workflow context.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>LlamaIndex</h1>
  <p class="lead">dotfetch plugs into LlamaIndex's agent workflows: a tool retriever that picks each step's tools, failures returned as error <code>ToolOutput</code>s, approval through workflow human-in-the-loop events, and the workflow <code>Context</code> for your state.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/llamaindex/advanced/">Advanced LlamaIndex usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "dotfetch[llamaindex]"   # llama-index-core >= 0.13`} />

  <h2>Basic page: tools picked every step</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from llama_index.llms.openai import OpenAI
from dotfetch import DotFetch
from dotfetch.llamaindex import LlamaIndexAdapter

fetcher = DotFetch()

@fetcher.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await fetcher.sync()
agent = LlamaIndexAdapter(fetcher).function_agent(OpenAI(model="gpt-5.5"), limit=5)
response = await agent.run(user_msg="Has order 4471 shipped?")`} />
  <p>For a fixed set, pass <code>FunctionAgent(tools=await adapter.select(query), llm=llm)</code> instead.</p>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call raises <code>LlamaIndexToolError</code>, whose text is <code>&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;</code> capped at 2,000 characters. The agent turns it into <code>ToolOutput(is_error=True)</code> and the model can try again.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>LlamaIndexAdapter(fetcher, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> raises the plain <code>ToolExecutionError</code>.</div>

  <h2>Reading workflow state from a dotfetch tool</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch.llamaindex import current_workflow_context

@fetcher.register
async def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    ctx = current_workflow_context()   # the workflow Context, or None for a direct call
    user = await ctx.store.get("user")
    return await bank.balance(user, account)`} />
